# The agent sandbox: a Python runtime, prime-agent, and nothing of this project.
#
# Build on a compute node, never a login node (this cluster has no `debug` partition; use an
# allocation you already hold, or `isi`). From the repo root:
#
#     module load apptainer
#     export APPTAINER_CACHEDIR=/scratch1/$USER/apptainer_cache TMPDIR=/scratch1/$USER/tmp
#     apptainer build --fakeroot <storage>/containers/sandbox-pa.sif containers/sandbox.def
#     bash containers/verify_sandbox.sh <storage>/containers/sandbox-pa.sif
#
# One core takes about ten minutes, most of it mksquashfs. The build needs the network.
#
# --fakeroot works here through a root-mapped namespace; this user has no /etc/subuid
# entry, so the subuid path is not available and that message at build time is expected.
#
# BOTH moving parts are pinned, because an unpinned one is a silent confound: two runs
# weeks apart would use different software with nothing in the record saying so.
#
#   - the base, by digest alone (Apptainer rejects a reference carrying both a tag and a
#     digest, so `python:3.12` survives only as a label). The previous image was built from the floating tag
#     `python:3.12`, which is not rebuildable; the digest below is the one that image
#     actually resolved to, read back off it with `apptainer inspect`.
#   - prime-agent, by PRIME_AGENT_VERSION, which makes the installer skip the `stable`
#     channel pointer. Unpinned it installs whatever is newest on the day of the build.
#
# prime-agent 0.10.3, linux-x64, is
#     releases/v0.10.3/prime-agent-0.10.3-linux-x64.tar.gz
#     sha256 811d9f0ec9dff007d5bda9c8435b0e7f46ef7041fa2fc103efc9edc295cb5528
# as published in <base>/latest.json. The installer verifies this itself against the
# manifest and SHA256SUMS and dies on a mismatch; it is recorded here so the expected
# bytes are in version control rather than only on someone's CDN.
#
# The installer is vendored (containers/prime_agent_install.sh) rather than fetched in
# %post, so the build runs the exact bytes that were reviewed:
#     sha256 75522795d5198152567dcf0c99f26faa4e8b2df0c40d285221bd71313142398c
#
# The image still needs the network at build time: the installer downloads the payload
# from the R2 base. A withdrawn version or an R2 outage fails the build.
#
# THE PYTHON KERNEL. prime-agent's python_repl tool runs in a kernel venv that it builds on
# first use with uv: CPython 3.11, its bundled prime-agent-runtime and skills, and twelve
# default packages with no versions given. Left to that, every fresh agent home downloads
# ~100 MB and resolves whatever is newest -- unpinned and network-dependent, per run. And
# without uv in the image it does not run at all: the kernel fails to start and the agent
# loses every tool that goes through Python.
#
# So the kernel is pinned and built here, at build time:
#   - uv 0.13.8, system-wide, so it is on PATH and the installer does not fetch an
#     unpinned one with curl;
#   - CPython 3.11.18 under /opt/pa-kernel/data/uv/python (read-only at runtime, which a
#     venv's base interpreter may be). prime-agent strips UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR, UV_PYTHON and
#     the other interpreter overrides before it runs uv (pa-core kernel/python_env.rs,
#     sanitize_uv_path), so a checked-out repo cannot redirect the kernel's Python. uv's
#     default location follows XDG_DATA_HOME instead, which is NOT stripped: it is set for the
#     build only, and the 3.11.18 put there first makes the bootstrap's own
#     `uv python install 3.11` -- which on its own means "newest 3.11" -- a no-op;
#   - the venv, by the installer's own kernel pre-warm (`prime-agent --prime-agent-bootstrap`),
#     so its .bootstrap-version file is exactly what prime-agent writes, with every package
#     held to containers/kernel_constraints.txt through UV_CONSTRAINT (which is not stripped);
#   - prime-agent's six bundled Python skills, which the pre-warm leaves out and a first
#     session would otherwise install over the network, unpinned. containers/
#     seed_kernel_skills.py runs prime-agent's own install command for them and records them
#     as prime-agent does, so a session finds nothing missing.
# It is built at HOME=/home/agent -- the path the harness mounts the agent home at -- so its
# absolute paths are the runtime ones, then moved to /opt/pa-kernel/seed-venv. The wrapper
# containers/prime_agent_wrapper.sh copies it into each fresh agent home on first use. It must
# be writable there: a read-only kernel (PRIME_AGENT_KERNEL_PYTHON) makes prime-agent disable
# every Python skill /refine creates, which would quietly break the carry memory mode.
#
# Only the kernel survives from that build HOME. Sessions, config and anything else the
# installer leaves under it are deleted: the kernel is a runtime, agent memory is not.

Bootstrap: docker
From: python@sha256:cad37dd20c7cac861af9003af8796d03ea7a998ec1e3a664429740fc9d7d2691

%files
    containers/prime_agent_install.sh /opt/build/install.sh
    containers/kernel_constraints.txt /opt/build/kernel_constraints.txt
    containers/kernel_skills.json /opt/build/kernel_skills.json
    containers/seed_kernel_skills.py /opt/build/seed_kernel_skills.py
    containers/prime_agent_wrapper.sh /opt/sandbox/bin/prime-agent
    containers/netbridge.py /opt/sandbox/bin/netbridge.py
    containers/sandbox_run.sh /opt/sandbox/bin/sandbox-run

%post
    set -eux

    # /opt/pa, not ~/.local: the image is read-only at runtime. The binary belongs to the
    # image; the agent's durable state does not.
    export PRIME_AGENT_RUST_PREFIX=/opt/pa
    export PRIME_AGENT_VERSION=0.10.3
    export PRIME_AGENT_TELEMETRY=0 DO_NOT_TRACK=1

    # uv, pinned and on PATH before the installer looks for one.
    python -m pip install --no-cache-dir uv==0.13.8
    uv --version

    # The kernel's interpreter, pinned, at a fixed read-only path; see the header for why
    # this is XDG_DATA_HOME and not UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR. Build-time only: at runtime the
    # agent's data home is its own, writable one.
    export XDG_DATA_HOME=/opt/pa-kernel/data
    export UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/uv-build-cache
    export UV_CONSTRAINT=/opt/build/kernel_constraints.txt
    uv python install 3.11.18

    # Built at the runtime agent-home path; see the header.
    export HOME=/home/agent
    mkdir -p "$HOME" /opt/pa

    sh /opt/build/install.sh

    # The installer's pre-warm is best-effort -- it warns and carries on if the kernel does
    # not build. Here a missing kernel is a broken image, so require it.
    /opt/pa/bin/prime-agent --version
    test -x "$HOME/.prime/agent/kernel-venv/bin/python"
    "$HOME/.prime/agent/kernel-venv/bin/python" -c "import rlm, dill, numpy, pandas, requests"
    # The venv's base interpreter must be the pinned one in the image, not one under $HOME,
    # which is deleted below and shadowed by the agent home at runtime.
    grep -qx "home = /opt/pa-kernel/data/uv/python/.*" "$HOME/.prime/agent/kernel-venv/pyvenv.cfg"
    "$HOME/.prime/agent/kernel-venv/bin/python" --version | grep -qx "Python 3.11.18"

    python /opt/build/seed_kernel_skills.py "$HOME/.prime/agent/kernel-venv" \
        /opt/build/kernel_skills.json /opt/pa/share/prime-agent/prime-agent-runtime

    mkdir -p /opt/pa-kernel
    mv "$HOME/.prime/agent/kernel-venv" /opt/pa-kernel/seed-venv
    uv pip freeze --python /opt/pa-kernel/seed-venv/bin/python > /opt/pa-kernel/freeze.txt
    chmod 0755 /opt/sandbox/bin/prime-agent /opt/sandbox/bin/sandbox-run

    # Of the build data home keep only the interpreter; of the build HOME keep nothing.
    find "$XDG_DATA_HOME" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name uv -exec rm -rf {} +
    find "$XDG_DATA_HOME/uv" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name python -exec rm -rf {} +
    rm -rf /opt/build "$HOME" "$UV_CACHE_DIR"

%environment
    export PATH=/opt/sandbox/bin:/opt/pa/bin:$PATH
    export PRIME_AGENT_TELEMETRY=0
    export DO_NOT_TRACK=1

%labels
    prime_agent.version 0.10.3
    prime_agent.platform linux-x64
    prime_agent.sha256 811d9f0ec9dff007d5bda9c8435b0e7f46ef7041fa2fc103efc9edc295cb5528
    prime_agent.prefix /opt/pa
    installer.sha256 75522795d5198152567dcf0c99f26faa4e8b2df0c40d285221bd71313142398c
    base.image python:3.12
    base.digest sha256:cad37dd20c7cac861af9003af8796d03ea7a998ec1e3a664429740fc9d7d2691
    kernel.uv 0.13.8
    kernel.python 3.11.18
    kernel.python_dir /opt/pa-kernel/data/uv/python
    kernel.skills agent_message,attach_image,compact,edit,goal,refine
    kernel.seed /opt/pa-kernel/seed-venv
    kernel.freeze /opt/pa-kernel/freeze.txt
    telemetry off
    sandbox.entry /opt/sandbox/bin/sandbox-run
    sandbox.network run with --net --network none; channels are bind-mounted unix sockets

%help
    The agent sandbox for GameBoyRL evaluation runs.

    prime-agent 0.10.3 is on PATH (through /opt/sandbox/bin/prime-agent, which seeds the
    pinned Python kernel into a fresh agent home). Its durable state (~/.prime, ~/.config) is
    NOT in the image: it lives in the writable agent home the harness mounts at /home/agent,
    one per run, which is what makes isolated and carry memory modes different from each other.
    Telemetry is off.

    Nothing of the GameBoyRL project is in this image. The workspace arrives on /work.

    Run it isolated: --net --network none gives it no network at all, and `sandbox-run`
    bridges exactly the channels named in SANDBOX_BRIDGE -- bind-mounted unix sockets for the
    env server (env_server/server.py --unix_socket) and the model gateway
    (env_server/model_gateway.py), which holds the API key on the host -- onto its private
    loopback. prime-agent reaches the gateway through a custom provider in
    ~/.prime/agent/models.json; envctl reaches the env server at ENV_SERVER_URL.
